---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, META_DESCRIPTIONS, SITE_NAME, SITE_URL } from "../config/site";

const canonicalUrl = `${SITE_URL}/privacy-policy/`;
const lastUpdated = "October 27, 2026";
---

<Layout
	title={`Privacy Policy — ${SITE_NAME}`}
	description={META_DESCRIPTIONS.privacy}
	canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl}
	robots="noindex,follow"
>
	<div class="page">
		<p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
		<h1 style="margin-top: var(--space-3)">Privacy Policy</h1>
		<p style="margin-top: var(--space-2); color: var(--ink-3)">
			Last updated: {lastUpdated}
		</p>

		<div class="panel policy" style="margin-top: var(--space-7)">
			<section class="policy-block">
				<h2>Overview</h2>
				<p class="lede">
					This website (<strong>{SITE_URL.replace("https://", "")}</strong>) is a static
					site for {SITE_NAME}. It has no user accounts, advertising, or mailing list. It
					has one contact form, and uses Google Analytics only if you opt in. This policy covers
					what happens when you visit, including the third-party services the site uses,
					links to, or embeds.
				</p>
			</section>

			<hr class="rule" />

			<section class="policy-block">
				<h2>Information We Collect</h2>
				<p class="lede">
					The site collects only what you choose to submit through the contact form: your
					name, email address, optional subject, and message. That information is used to
					receive and respond to your enquiry. It is not added to a mailing list, sold, or
					stored in a website database.
				</p>
			</section>

			<hr class="rule" />

			<section class="policy-block">
				<h2>Contact Form</h2>
				<p class="lede">
					When you send the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>, Cloudflare Turnstile
					checks the submission for automated abuse. Cloudflare receives your IP address
					and technical signals from your browser for that check. The form contents are
					then sent through Cloudflare Email Sending to the site's inbox and kept only as
					long as needed for the resulting correspondence.
				</p>
			</section>

			<hr class="rule" />

			<section class="policy-block">
				<h2>Hosting</h2>
				<p class="lede">
					This site is hosted on <strong>Cloudflare Workers</strong>. Like most web hosts,
					Cloudflare's infrastructure processes standard request data (such as IP
					address, user agent, and request timing) to serve pages and protect against
					abuse. Separately, the site uses Google Analytics, described below.
					See the <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare Privacy Policy<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.
				</p>
			</section>

			<hr class="rule" />

			<section class="policy-block">
				<h2>Analytics</h2>
				<p class="lede">
					This site can use <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> to count visits and see
					which pages are viewed, but only if you agree. On your first visit a banner
					asks. Until you accept, the Google tag is never loaded: no analytics cookies
					are set and no request is made to Google, so nothing about your visit reaches
					them. Declining takes one click, and the site works exactly the same either way.
				</p>
				<p class="lede" style="margin-top: var(--space-4)">
					If you accept, the tag sets cookies (such as <code>_ga</code>) and reports
					information about your visit to Google: pages viewed, approximate location
					derived from your IP address, browser, device type, and referring site. Google
					processes it under its own
					<a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy terms<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.
					We use it to understand how the site is used, not to identify individuals or
					for advertising, and it is not sold or combined with anything else collected here.
				</p>
				<p class="lede" style="margin-top: var(--space-4)">
					Your answer is remembered in your browser's local storage, not in a cookie. You
					can change it at any time with the <button
						type="button"
						class="inline-link-button"
						data-cookie-preferences>Cookie choices</button
					> link in the footer of any page. Withdrawing consent deletes the analytics
					cookies and reloads the page. Ad and tracker blockers and Google's <a
						href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout"
						target="_blank"
						rel="noopener noreferrer">opt-out add-on<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a
					> also work.
				</p>
			</section>

			<hr class="rule" />

			<section class="policy-block">
				<h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
				<p class="lede">
					This site loads or links to a small number of third-party services that may
					collect data independently under their own privacy policies:
				</p>
				<ul class="policy-list">
					<li>
						<strong>Google Analytics</strong> — loaded only if you accept the cookie
						banner, as described above. See the
						<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Cloudflare Turnstile and Email Sending</strong> — used to protect the
						contact form from automated abuse and deliver submitted messages. See the
						<a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare Privacy Policy<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong> — Cloudflare, our host, adds a small
						script that measures page views and load performance. It does not use cookies
						or track you across sites, and it loads regardless of the cookie banner. See the
						<a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare Privacy Policy<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Fonts</strong> — the site's typefaces are served from this site
						itself, so loading them sends nothing to Google or any other third party.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Spotify</strong> — the homepage offers a Spotify album player so
						you can preview the record without leaving the site. If you accept the cookie
						banner, the player loads with the page. Otherwise it loads only after you
						click "Load the Spotify player", and until then nothing is requested from
						Spotify. Withdrawing consent reloads the page without the player. Once loaded, Spotify's player may set its own cookies and collect
						usage data, including your IP address. We also link to our Spotify artist
						profile elsewhere. See the
						<a href="https://www.spotify.com/legal/privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Spotify Privacy Policy<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Apple Music</strong> — we link to our Apple Music artist profile.
						Apple may collect data if you visit their platform. See the
						<a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apple Privacy Policy<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<hr class="rule" />

			<section class="policy-block">
				<h2>Cookies</h2>
				<p class="lede">
					This site does not set advertising cookies. Google Analytics cookies are set
					only if you accept them, as described above. The Spotify
					player may set its own cookies once it loads, which happens only if you accept
					the banner or click to load it, subject to Spotify's
					privacy policy above. Cloudflare may use strictly necessary storage while
					protecting the contact form. You can control or delete cookies through your
					browser settings.
				</p>
			</section>

			<hr class="rule" />

			<section class="policy-block">
				<h2>External Links</h2>
				<p class="lede">
					This site links to external platforms (Spotify, Apple Music, Instagram, TikTok,
					Facebook, X, and others as they're added). We're not responsible for the privacy
					practices or content of those sites.
				</p>
			</section>

			<hr class="rule" />

			<section class="policy-block">
				<h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
				<p class="lede">
					We may update this policy as the site changes — for example, if new streaming
					or social platforms are added. Any changes will be reflected on this page with
					an updated date.
				</p>
			</section>

			<hr class="rule" />

			<section class="policy-block">
				<h2>Contact</h2>
				<p class="lede">
					For privacy-related questions, use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>. If
					the form is unavailable, the page displays
					<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> as a fallback.
				</p>
			</section>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.policy {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
	}

	.policy-block h2 {
		font-size: var(--text-h3);
		margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
	}

	.policy .rule {
		margin: var(--space-6) 0;
	}

	.policy-list {
		margin: var(--space-4) 0 0;
		padding-left: 1.25em;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: var(--space-3);
		color: var(--ink-2);
		font-size: var(--text-body-lg);
		line-height: var(--lh-body);
	}
</style>
